ate:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T10:22:43-08:00","id":406816,"title":"","content":"Let's be fair, putting the God machine on the level of Luna is higher then &quot;big monster.&quot; We're looking at godly stuff then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T14:28:33-08:00","id":406972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=406816#post406816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's be fair, putting the God machine on the level of Luna is higher then &amp;quot;big monster.&amp;quot; We're looking at godly stuff then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, it's like Luna or the Exarchs, a cosmic threat. Still not something that has anything approaching omnipotence or omniscience, and even if it exists in your Werewolf game it probably only rarely overlaps with the spiritual niche of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T14:34:10-08:00","id":406997,"title":"","content":"Luna isn't really a threat. More of a patron, or if you're a member of the Pure, something to rail against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T14:46:08-08:00","id":407018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=406997#post406997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna isn't really a threat. More of a patron, or if you're a member of the Pure, something to rail against.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was more to emphasize the scope that all these beings exist on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T23:43:51-08:00","id":407456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=406997#post406997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna isn't really a threat. More of a patron, or if you're a member of the Pure, something to rail against.</div> </div> </div> </div>She's an unknowable entity, worshipped by a cult of murderous shapeshifting war machines, who do what they think is her bidding as passed down by her insane quicksilver spirit servants, while also guided by monstrous predatory wolf spirits with their own agendas.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Luna is a threat, just maybe, *maybe* not to the Forsaken. (As a race. Her expectations are a threat to the survivability of individuals.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 02-16-2015, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T01:02:59-08:00","id":407496,"title":"","content":"Dont forget that twilight is not a place or a realm, its a state of being. There is actually no reason why angels and spirits should be able to see each other by default. The only things they have in common is that they are invisible and intangible for the rest of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T03:02:04-08:00","id":407541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's be fair, putting the God machine on the level of Luna is higher then &quot;big monster.&quot; We're looking at godly stuff then. </div> </div> </div>Luna is part of a line which is based on ideas of animism and polytheism. Therefore her being one among a multitude of deities in the Shadow works great. With the God-machine, going right back to that first story in the core and onwards, it's riffing on ideas about monotheism. The aesthetic is that the God-machine is the secret truth behind the world. And the more you restrain that idea and make exceptions to it, I think it damages that overall aesthetic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T05:56:13-08:00","id":407623,"title":"","content":"Speaking of, I don't know, sensing weird things, is there a wolf-blooded tell that grants said mortal an Uratha's heightened senses?<br /> <br /> I didn't really want to create a topic just for that or necro anything, so I figured this was the best I'll get <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T08:13:15-08:00","id":407773,"title":"","content":"I think dalu form helps with that... But probably","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T08:28:49-08:00","id":407782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=407541#post407541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the God-machine, going right back to that first story in the core and onwards, it's riffing on ideas about monotheism. The aesthetic is that the God-machine is the secret truth behind the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>The facts that <i>qashmalim</i> are a corebook thing and the Machine's provenance is in-universe speculated in a variety of ways to be formerly part of a larger structure would seem to put the lie to both of these. &quot;God knows more cheat-codes than any of us, has the establishment mostly on Its side, and wants to break us down for parts&quot; is of a greater concern to the Unchained than any claim that there aren't other deities around that by definition would probably be less interested in them in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T17:06:18-08:00","id":408333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=406028#post406028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you can keep your games separate.</div> </div> </div> </div>And <i><b>why </b></i>does that <i><b>require </b></i>separate &quot;Frequencies&quot; of Twilight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T17:08:47-08:00","id":408337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=406194#post406194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For one, it makes Twilight less crowded. If spirits, ghosts, angels, etc. all exist in the same frequency, this would imply a lot of interaction between them as they would run into each other all the time. The split helps you to, for example, have ghost stories without having to take spirits into account, while still acknowledging the existence of spirits in your game world. Also, when you want the different types to interact, it is possible. It just isn't the default anymore, so when it happens it is something out of the ordinary (or something worth investigating, when for example the whole local spirit population feeds on ghosts).<br /> <br /> The split doesn't actually dramatically change the powers of player character, as a lot of powers already interacted only with one type of ephemeral entity. Now these powers interact only with one type of Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry... I just don't buy that explanation. I still don't really see a <i><b>NEED </b></i>for them to be separate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T17:11:36-08:00","id":408339,"title":"","content":"Otherwise you could have your totem destroy ghosts for you, or be destroyed by angels. Or your God Machine or haunted house mystery could be solved simply because the players' totem can see everything going on in Twilight.<br /> <br /> Instead, things work off their own frequency and only share the same spot if you want them to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T17:11:42-08:00","id":408340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gflash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=407496#post407496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dont forget that twilight is not a place or a realm, its a state of being. There is actually no reason why angels and spirits should be able to see each other by default. The only things they have in common is that they are invisible and intangible for the rest of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't share realms, though, and that is the point. <i><b>Only in Twilight or the Manifest World </b></i>can they interact with each other, unless I have missed something along the way, which is possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T17:18:10-08:00","id":408343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=408340#post408340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't share realms, though, and that is the point. <i><b>Only in Twilight or the Manifest World </b></i>can they interact with each other, unless I have missed something along the way, which is possible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Twilight isn't a realm, it is a state of being in the manifest world and possibly other worlds. I don't know if you read comics, so this might not help, but it's like vibrating at a different frequency than the real world, so that you can move through it unseen and unhindered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T21:50:39-08:00","id":408598,"title":"","content":"I like the different separate Twilight frequencies personally, because I like being able to have ghost heavy stories (including those with Sin Eaters), spirit heavy stories (like Werewolf), etc. without necessarily having to account for the other options; I especially like that when they -do- crossover, it's something that's actually pretty notable, like when a Bone Shadow uses a rite to pierce the veil of death to see ghosts.<br /> <br /> Personally I track somewhere between half a dozen and a dozen different flavors of Twilight, but I'm weird; I think it's really a non-issue since outside of edge cases people were already dealing with only a certain subset of ephemeral being in a given game and 1e powers already mostly featured or prioritized interaction with those same subsets. To me the emphasis on different frequencies in 2e is mostly a clarification that makes it easy to understand right out of the gate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T06:59:51-08:00","id":408924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=408343#post408343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Twilight isn't a realm, it is a state of being in the manifest world and possibly other worlds. I don't know if you read comics, so this might not help, but it's like vibrating at a different frequency than the real world, so that you can move through it unseen and unhindered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that Twilight is not a Realm, but the Shadow is, the Underworld is, etc. Twilight is a state of being that those from other realms share when in the physical realm, but not materialized. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And I understand Frequencies. I get that. But you still have yet to show <i><b>WHY </b></i>there needs be <i><b>different frequencies </b></i>of Twilight. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Twilight is not so crowded as to need that distinction, in my opinion. In my games, Twilight is just Twilight - it is a shared state of being, because there is not reason it cannot be. That is what I am asking here... <i><b>WHY </b></i>does it need to be distinct for each of the various entities?<br /> <br /> @ <i><b>Kirby Jerusalem</b></i>... In my opinion, having separate frequencies actually muddies the waters, so to speak. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 02-17-2015, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T07:57:20-08:00","id":408973,"title":"","content":"Because the writers wanted to have different frequencies, if you want to get right down to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T08:06:38-08:00","id":408979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=406012#post406012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, no. Ok.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uratha do have some tools in their armoury against non-spirit entities like angels, ghosts, mages, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T08:08:07-08:00","id":408981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=408924#post408924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand that Twilight is not a Realm, but the Shadow is, the Underworld is, etc. Twilight is a state of being that those from other realms share when in the physical realm, but not materialized. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And I understand Frequencies. I get that. But you still have yet to show <i><b>WHY </b></i>there needs be <i><b>different frequencies </b></i>of Twilight. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Twilight is not so crowded as to need that distinction, in my opinion. In my games, Twilight is just Twilight - it is a shared state of being, because there is not reason it cannot be. That is what I am asking here... <i><b>WHY </b></i>does it need to be distinct for each of the various entities?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F54rqDh2mWA\" target=\"_blank\">Oh the humanity!</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=408973#post408973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the writers wanted to have different frequencies, if you want to get right down to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I endorse that feature as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T09:38:42-08:00","id":409054,"title":"","content":"Something to keep in mind about Twilight.<br /> <br /> It is heavily, heavily, heavily populated by ghosts. I mean, for every spirit that pops over into Twilight, you have a large number of ghosts already there, as well as a significant number of ghost buildings and objects. <br /> <br /> So, you want to mesh all the different ephemeral beings into one joint area? Then your werewolf games would effectively end up being turned into a Geist game. You would be seeing ghosts everywhere, who'd want you to do stuff for them once they realized it. Worse, we then get into the parts where we have to ask about how werewolves would be hunting ghosts. Would they? Do they? Most of them aren't hunt-worthy, I imagine. So, what does that mean for wolves who are constantly around them? <br /> <br /> It would detract from the very nature of the game. The Wolf Must Hunt. Not, The Wolf Must Double As Mediums For Ghosts. Or, The Wolf Must Wage War Against God. Or The Wolf Must Solve Mental Problem-Projections Running Amok.<br /> <br /> That is why they need to be distinct. Because otherwise, it would ruin the games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T10:05:18-08:00","id":409069,"title":"","content":"Although in some places, like the UK described in Shadows of the United Kingdom, having a ton of ghosts around is actually pretty cool (and described in detail).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T08:41:50-08:00","id":410127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=409054#post409054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to keep in mind about Twilight.<br /> <br /> It is heavily, heavily, heavily populated by ghosts. I mean, for every spirit that pops over into Twilight, you have a large number of ghosts already there, as well as a significant number of ghost buildings and objects.<br /> <br /> So, you want to mesh all the different ephemeral beings into one joint area? Then your werewolf games would effectively end up being turned into a Geist game. You would be seeing ghosts everywhere, who'd want you to do stuff for them once they realized it. Worse, we then get into the parts where we have to ask about how werewolves would be hunting ghosts. Would they? Do they? Most of them aren't hunt-worthy, I imagine. So, what does that mean for wolves who are constantly around them?<br /> <br /> It would detract from the very nature of the game. The Wolf Must Hunt. Not, The Wolf Must Double As Mediums For Ghosts. Or, The Wolf Must Wage War Against God. Or The Wolf Must Solve Mental Problem-Projections Running Amok.<br /> <br /> That is why they need to be distinct. Because otherwise, it would ruin the games.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, when I read the books, I don't see what you emphasized... Heavily, Heavily, Heavily populated with Ghosts? Just don't see it. <br /> The different ephemerals are there for providing story points. If your werewolf games centers around ghosts, there will be ghosts... if your vampire game centers around spiritual influences, there will be spiritual influences; yadda yadda yadda. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> I apparently just do not see things the way that you do. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> No worries, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T09:35:18-08:00","id":410208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=406194#post406194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just isn't the default anymore, so when it happens it is something out of the ordinary (or something worth investigating, when for example the whole local spirit population feeds on ghosts).</div> </div> </div> </div>As it stood, with one &quot;frequency,&quot; would have to be a specific reason the Werewolf mythos <i>didn't</i> constantly try to mug the Geist mythos for essence. (Though I get round that by breaking up the types of energy).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T10:51:54-08:00","id":410322,"title":"","content":"Something cool to have in a werewolf game, is a merit that allows their spirit sense to pick up other types of ephemerals. So if there were a territory that was threatened by ghosts all the time, rather than spirits, the were wolves could adapt to that situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T11:15:29-08:00","id":410350,"title":"","content":"I think we've been told there's a way to see ghosts, if not I'd be very surprised if one didn't exist.<br /> <br /> Other stuff, angels and demons and other demons are likely to pop up further down the line. There's probably Lodges to hunt GM Angels and GM Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T11:38:15-08:00","id":410380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=410127#post410127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, when I read the books, I don't see what you emphasized... Heavily, Heavily, Heavily populated with Ghosts? Just don't see it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its something that I've personally come to realize when talking to the writers when it comes to the Moros and Geist as a game. It may be a fault of the writing to not clearly convey it, but that's the intent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The different ephemerals are there for providing story points. If your werewolf games centers around ghosts, there will be ghosts... if your vampire game centers around spiritual influences, there will be spiritual influences; yadda yadda yadda. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div> There's a HUGE difference between a storyteller deciding to play to a niche concept, and something being central to a game by design. Having werewolves see astral entities, ghosts, infernal demons, and angels all the time undermines the core themes of Werewolf as a game. <br /> <br /> In 2e, there's not even a way for vampires to really deal with spirits yet! So, dealing with spiritual influences is going to be really difficult there. A storyteller can try to force it, of course, but its clearly not a focus nor intent of the game. The core vampire game has its own themes and designs where spiritual influences isn't really a big part of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T14:54:20-08:00","id":410553,"title":"","content":"As I said - Different Viewpoints...<br /> <br /> And honestly, if the writers fell down on the exposition of their intent, well, we only have what they wrote... Or is it your extrapolation of what they wrote, and it does not line up with your POV, because you prefer a far more numerous population of ephemeral entities always surrounding humanity? Because honestly, I have never seen anything close to what you are referring to in any of the books (though I do not possess them all).<br /> <br /> Besides, If I want to tell a ghost story and the players want to play werewolves or vampires, then more power to them, it will work (etcetera yadda yadda), even if it takes more effort on my part. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also, I don't see the various ephemerals as niche concepts (so in that we differ greatly) the way that you apparently do. Especially if you are running a crossover game in any capacity.<br /> <br /> As for what a certain splat sees in Twilight (take your Werewolf example from above), what makes you think that they will be inundated with visuals of Demons, Infernals, Ghosts, Spirits and Angels? My Twilight is obviously FAR less crowded than yours is, and they will generally only encounter what they look for. As werewolves, they will obviously interact with Spirits (probably more in the Shadow than in the Physical/Twilight), but if I am running a story where there are Ghosts, then they will also interact with Ghosts. Again, etcetera. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They might also catch sight of something that they do not understand, and again, they may not. Nothing forces you to use all the denizens at once, nor do they need to be so numerous that they are all bumping into each other like a horde of lemmings tumbling over a cliff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And you can even go with a shared Twilight, and have various abilities (whether inherent or learned) that allow one to see the various ephemerals. There is absolutely no reason (in my opinion) for them to be split over different frequencies. *shrug*<br /> <br /> And as a note - I don't run 2nd Edition... I far prefer Original nWOD, or the FATE port that I have been putting together. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 02-18-2015, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T16:38:14-08:00","id":410731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=410553#post410553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as a note - I don't run 2nd Edition... I far prefer Original nWOD, or the FATE port that I have been putting together. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you've said so multiple times. Because you've popped into discussions of 2e multiple times to complain about it. Knowing as you do that those discussions are about 2e.<br /> <br /> It's very obnoxious and more than a little futile, to be frank. If you're actually open to being convinced, that's one thing, but you just seeming to be trying to pick an argument on this particular issue. Nobody's going to change your mind and your points are neither new nor convincing in themselves. Save everybody some time, please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T07:29:44-08:00","id":411459,"title":"","content":"Hey - I love the 2nd edition fluff... Just have issues with the Mechanics. What we are talking about here is Fluff. So I feel justified in having a say in the matter. *shrug*<br /> I just do not see any rationale yet to accept different frequencies of Twilight. No one has actually made any convincing arguments other than &quot;My interpretation of the devs opinions&quot; - which are not backed up by what they wrote so you will just have to take my opinion as fact.&quot; You have Others (non-Devs) speaking to the Dev's intent... forgive me if I disregard such tactics.<br /> Maybe you have something convincing that might sway me, Satchel? Or maybe not? Oh well, I shall still look to the discussion, then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Just because you do not agree with me does not mean that someone does not hold some of the same ideas as I do. Deal with it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 02-19-2015, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T07:48:43-08:00","id":411472,"title":"","content":"Somebody remembers how to set users to be ignored in these forums? I could use that knowledge.<br /> <br /> There, everything is awesomer now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 02-19-2015, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T09:39:21-08:00","id":411689,"title":"","content":"Kinda rude, since I am looking for an answer that is better than &quot;because.&quot; Oh well... *shrug*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T07:40:43-08:00","id":415132,"title":"","content":"You know I'm going to have to agree with Tymeaus Jalynsfein on this one. Crowded is that last word I would every use to describe Twilight. I've always been under the impression that Ephemeral Entities were rare. With local populations depending largely on local conditions. Spirits being far more common in areas with weak Gauntlets, or actual holes in the Gauntlet. Ghost are a deeply personal kind of being, and will be hidden away in a deeply personal location keeping them outside of random encounter status. I wasn't even aware that Astral Entities could even get to the material world without some form of summoning. Angels and Quashmallin are super rare in their own rights, with Quashmallin only appearing as a plot point, and I always thought that Angels were far more likely to be hanging out disguised as Material Humans than filling up space as Twilight entities.<br /> <br /> Finally, Mage gets really awkward with multiple Twilight states. A Mage needs to be able to see an Ephemeral entity and now know what it is by just checking Twilight Frequency. The Mae needs to be able to poke at it and examine it, study and Learn.<br /> <br /> Werewolf never suffered from a shared Twilight state. The Spirits they hunt need to be rare enough that it can be called a hunt, and not farming. Everything else is rare enough that you only need to encounter it if plot demands it. If you really want to find Spirits go to the Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T15:35:16-08:00","id":415787,"title":"","content":"Actually ghosts seem to be very common but most are like broken records barely Rank 1. But there are lots of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T00:23:08-08:00","id":416250,"title":"","content":"Lots of dead humans after all. Oh another situation that ended in Kuruth in a grocery store? Shit theres 30 souls with unfinished business right there! (I have no idea if that's how ghosts work in NWoD)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T01:20:25-08:00","id":416284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=415132#post415132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crowded is that last word I would every use to describe Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be if all Twilight entities were on one &quot;frequency&quot;.<br /> <br /> Ghosts, Spirits, Abyssal Intruders, Infernal Demons, God-Machine Angels, God-Machine Demons, Auspex and Mind Projections, Death and Spirit mages, Sin-Eaters, Tulpas, mortals with various kinds of relics or supernatural boons... and that list is not even exhaustive by a mile. Not to mention ghostly buildings and Twilight Infrastructure, which would be even harder to ignore or miss.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=415132#post415132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ghost are a deeply personal kind of being, and will be hidden away in a deeply personal location</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the kid who got run over by a car on an open street. Or the gangbanger banging his last after a shoot-out. Or any place in a city that has seen a major war or plague.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=415132#post415132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Angels and Quashmallin are super rare in their own rights</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps so, but when they are around, having your Mekhet or Mastigos, zooming over the city in an astral body, not notice that Seraph blazing like the sun seems a bit silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=415132#post415132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything else is rare enough that you only need to encounter it if plot demands it. If you really want to find Spirits go to the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you argue this, you basically make it a moot point. Whether Twilight is shared or not does not matter if you argue that it should only come up &quot;when the plot demands it&quot;. However, by making it multiple frequencies by default, the developers circumvent a major potential source of broken disbelief in players well-versed in the various WoD gamelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":". 02-23-2015, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T01:30:52-08:00","id":416290,"title":"","content":"Since there are enough spirits to conquer or destroy the world as we know it if werewolves didn't pull off their batman-esque &quot;I am the night!&quot; routine, yes I'd say twilight could get pretty darn crowded.<br /> <br /> And Hark, mages have death to deal with ghosts, spirit to deal with spirits, prime to sense quashmallam, mind to deal with goetia, five different arcanum to deal with supernal entities depending on what &quot;realm&quot; they come from, and who knows what arcanum they will need to deal with angels, frequency of twilight is the least of their worries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T14:52:21-08:00","id":416911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=416250#post416250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of dead humans after all. Oh another situation that ended in Kuruth in a grocery store? Shit theres 30 souls with unfinished business right there! (I have no idea if that's how ghosts work in NWoD)</div> </div> </div> </div>All dead humans do not generate Ghosts...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T16:15:27-08:00","id":416956,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/290897-classifying-twilight\">Didn't we have this argument before?<br /> <br /> And it went on for, like, 8 pages?</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/290897-classifying-twilight?p=291211#post291211\">I remember trotting out set theory at one point?</a><br /> <br /> Good times.<br /> <br /> I'm <i>still</i> of the opinion that having a Grand Unified Twilight is kinda <i>boring</i>.<br /> <br /> (Plus, Vampires do have the ability to interact with Spirits, a <i>leetle</i> bit. Namely, <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/\" target=\"_blank\">Khaibit</a> can see them, and Vampires can still perform all the actions mortals can with regards to Abjuring/Warding/Summoning. Just sayin'.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T04:41:29-08:00","id":417430,"title":"","content":"The notion behind separating out Twilight into different frequencies isn't just about affecting how different types of supernatural creature are able to perceive Twilight beings; it's also about affecting the interaction between different types of Twilight being with each other. Both are important elements to the change that occurred with Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T09:52:38-08:00","id":418839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=417430#post417430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The notion behind separating out Twilight into different frequencies isn't just about affecting how different types of supernatural creature are able to perceive Twilight beings; it's also about affecting the interaction between different types of Twilight being with each other. Both are important elements to the change that occurred with Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this is a change brought about by Second Edition? That may be the disconnect that I am having then (don't have any 2nd Edition Books, really - Dark Eras will be my first). If so, that would explain it. Thanks. Still don't see a need for it, but at least now I know why all the books I have been reading don't mention it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T09:56:12-08:00","id":418847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=416956#post416956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/290897-classifying-twilight\">Didn't we have this argument before?<br /> <br /> And it went on for, like, 8 pages?</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/290897-classifying-twilight?p=291211#post291211\">I remember trotting out set theory at one point?</a><br /> <br /> Good times.<br /> <br /> I'm <i>still</i> of the opinion that having a Grand Unified Twilight is kinda <i>boring</i>.<br /> <br /> (Plus, Vampires do have the ability to interact with Spirits, a <i>leetle</i> bit. Namely, <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/\" target=\"_blank\">Khaibit</a> can see them, and Vampires can still perform all the actions mortals can with regards to Abjuring/Warding/Summoning. Just sayin'.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Did we? I must have missed it - Will have to catch up on it... Thanks for the Link.<br /> EDIT: Wow... Looks like a Bag of Cats... But at least I am not alone in my opinion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 02-25-2015, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:39:01-08:00","id":419618,"title":"","content":"Guess when I ask questions in a forum I should specify if I mean 1e or 2e. I just assumed we'd all be on 2e mindset, also that the lore hadn't changed that much involving the hisil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T07:03:32-08:00","id":420119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=418839#post418839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So this is a change brought about by Second Edition? That may be the disconnect that I am having then (don't have any 2nd Edition Books, really - Dark Eras will be my first). If so, that would explain it. Thanks. Still don't see a need for it, but at least now I know why all the books I have been reading don't mention it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is explicitly a Second Edition thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T08:06:00-08:00","id":420207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=418839#post418839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this is a change brought about by Second Edition? That may be the disconnect that I am having then (don't have any 2nd Edition Books, really - Dark Eras will be my first). If so, that would explain it. Thanks. Still don't see a need for it, but at least now I know why all the books I have been reading don't mention it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really just a 2E change. 2E is making it explicit, but there's always been material that implied it worked that way. For example, werewolves need to purchase a gift to see ghosts in Twilight, whereas seeing spirits is innate. Mage spells are even more explicit, needing different Arcana to clearly see ghosts, spirits, mental projections, etc (although, at least in the case of Death and Spirit, it allows them to see the other being as a blurry, vague figure with a -3 perception penalty). Even in Second Sight, Thaumaturges have to buy See Spirits and See Ghosts separately, and their mental projections could only see other astral projections, unless they had See Ghosts or Spirits.<br /> <br /> Very few places I've seen imply that there's a unified Twilight. Immortals kind of does with the Purified innately seeing both, but they're supposed to be heavily tied to both, and they can't innately see anything else. In Book of Spirits, there's a coyote spirit which eats ghosts, but has a special Numen to do so.<br /> <br /> It would be confusing if just about every published set of powers treated different ephemera separately but all those beings existed in the same Twilight. It also doesn't matter, in the perspective of mechanics, since player templates need to buy different powers to see them all. All it would allow is for different ephemera to interact with each other more easily - and if you want to talk about complicated, deciding how every ephemeral antagonist responds to every other in the middle of your story takes the cake; it'd be like drawing a whole Classic WoD style conspiracy web. But maybe you're into that - and nothing is stopping you from doing that in your game. WoD is toolbox system, remember, that's why we love it. It's just that (almost) all of the published material pretty well implies they're separate; 2E is just saying it clearly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T08:49:29-08:00","id":420271,"title":"","content":"Strix in twilight are mentioned to be able to feed on both ghosts and spirits, so I guess some things can straddle frequencies. Then again they always were a bit odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T09:27:00-08:00","id":420326,"title":"","content":"While seeing them has required special abilities, spirits and ghosts were able to interact with each other in Twilight without any special requirements since the Werewolf core book.<br /> <br /> 'A ghost and a spirit can see, touch or otherwise interact with one another, as they are in the same ephemeral state.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T09:27:16-08:00","id":420327,"title":"","content":"Noteworthy, but I don't think that beings which straddle frequencies complicate the argument; if anything, I'd consider that support: they wouldn't go out of their way to write that if it was 'just Twilight'. If there are different frequencies, powers can exist which can pick and choose which ones are interacted with. Inclusion is easy, both mechanically and metaphysically. It stretches things more to say that Twilight's unified, but said being <i>can't</i> interact with these types.<br /> <br /> Storytellers <i>can</i> limit a unified Twilight just by saying &quot;that doesn't exist in my setting&quot; or controlling the numbers to their liking - clearly. But what is not accounted for is Storytellers who want to include various types of being, but don't want them to interact with each other, or don't want the players to sense them as easily. Exclusion is tougher to explain.<br /> <br /> A Twilight of different frequencies <i>easily </i>allows <i>more options</i> - and that's the way WoD's toolbox is meant to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 02-26-2015, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T09:54:55-08:00","id":420391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=420326#post420326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While seeing them has required special abilities, spirits and ghosts were able to interact with each other in Twilight without any special requirements since the Werewolf core book.<br /> <br /> 'A ghost and a spirit can see, touch or otherwise interact with one another, as they are in the same ephemeral state.' <b>(sidebar, pg 252)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>... A good point. That is a very solid wrench in my argument. Well then, I guess, 'screw it'?<br /> I had not remembered that quote. My apologies.<br /> <br /> I will just stand with my argument above, let it be a 1E vs 2E thing, and bow out gracefully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 02-26-2015, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T10:07:58-08:00","id":420404,"title":"","content":"There's a lot more ephemeral entities now than there was in the original books. I think it's still an appropriate change but does sort of manage to limit Werewolf's interactions with other games. If some lodges end up giving specific sacred prey you could probably overcome it so that there are lodges of angel hunters, demon hunters, strix and Goetic demon and abyssal hunters, each being granted the ability to see or at least sense their specific prey. Or you could just use the easy trick of saying things like angels, demons, strix and so forth are just spirits or hosts that have abilities to hide from werewolves in Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T10:32:58-08:00","id":420419,"title":"","content":"Yeah, WTF was like the second line they did, so back then twilight <i>was</i> sparse enough for the spirits and ghosts to coexist without much trouble. <br /> <br /> And I think there should definitely be exceptions to the general rule. Death spirits should probably be able to muck around with ghosts, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T10:36:52-08:00","id":420424,"title":"","content":"No more than it would limit Geist - or Changeling for that matter. Most of the games currently focus on one type of ephemeral threat (mage and hunter being the main exceptions) - and that's fine; it's tailored to the themes of those games, and most of them have an optional ability to interact with other types of beings if you want a specialist with more scope.<br /> <br /> While you could use the &quot;easy trick&quot; of saying all ephemera's the same, they can just hide from you, the metaphysics behind that choice is something that should be accounted for - and saying that is kind of wonky. Why can they hide - is it a numen they all have; is it just from werewolves; do they also hide from spirits, because shouldn't the half-spirit part of werewolves help them out with that? Mechanically it may work out the same, but the reasons <i>why </i>are just as important, and players will feel cheated without good reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T10:42:06-08:00","id":420429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=420419#post420419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, WTF was like the second line they did, so back then twilight <i>was</i> sparse enough for the spirits and ghosts to coexist without much trouble.<br /> <br /> And I think there should definitely be exceptions to the general rule. Death spirits should probably be able to muck around with ghosts, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was unfortunately lost in editing for space, but the Essence Thief Numen is supposed to give the entity the ability to percieve the type of essence it gains the ability to eat - a Spirit that can eat ghosts thanks to the Numen is able to see things in ghost-Twilight.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T11:20:50-08:00","id":420462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=420429#post420429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was unfortunately lost in editing for space, but the Essence Thief Numen is supposed to give the entity the ability to percieve the type of essence it gains the ability to eat - a Spirit that can eat ghosts thanks to the Numen is able to see things in ghost-Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>That answers that. Is this in reference to the GMC update, too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T11:25:38-08:00","id":420467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=420424#post420424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No more than it would limit Geist - or Changeling for that matter. Most of the games currently focus on one type of ephemeral threat (mage and hunter being the main exceptions) - and that's fine; it's tailored to the themes of those games, and most of them have an optional ability to interact with other types of beings if you want a specialist with more scope.<br /> <br /> While you could use the &quot;easy trick&quot; of saying all ephemera's the same, they can just hide from you, the metaphysics behind that choice is something that should be accounted for - and saying that is kind of wonky. Why can they hide - is it a numen they all have; is it just from werewolves; do they also hide from spirits, because shouldn't the half-spirit part of werewolves help them out with that? Mechanically it may work out the same, but the reasons <i>why </i>are just as important, and players will feel cheated without good reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are True Fae ephemerals? As far as I remember Changeling's only interaction with Twilight is through a contract.<br /> <br /> The issue is that the Shadow and Underworld are cross-splat concepts. Demons can speak and understand the First Tongue and the God Machine is specifically said to move spirits around in lieu of the most power-costly angels when it needs something done. Circle of the Crone blood sorcery and other disciplines interact with and mix the lines between spirit and vampire. But with the different frequencies, it keeps Werewolf from using things from other games, such as angels and strix. As I said, it's an appropriate change, but since the population of any ephemeral is purely up to the storyteller, it doesn't seem like that is the reason why the rule was changed.<br /> <br /> As for the reason for why things can't be seen while still being hunted, that was just an example and there's no reason anyone would have to keep themselves confined to it. If werewolves could recognize angels as being ephemerals they might think they're corrupted spirits. If they could recognize strix, they might think of them as another host, their darkness concealing them in Twilight. Both could be lesser avatars of a more powerful idigam. They have no presence in Twilight because they only exist when the avatar is manifested. The 'why' of the matter is unimportant for this discussion, which focuses on game mechanics, because the possible answers are infinite and never matter until a player's character asks why in-game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-26-2015, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T11:31:23-08:00","id":420488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=420462#post420462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That answers that. Is this in reference to the GMC update, too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm talking about the second edition Numen; I can't even remember if it was called that in first edition, or if there was a specific &quot;ghost-eater&quot; Numen. Either way, we put it in GMC for things like Death spirits, psychopomp-angels, or the rarer and stranger things like astral ghosts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T11:33:45-08:00","id":420501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=420467#post420467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are True Fae ephemerals? As far as I remember Changeling's only interaction with Twilight is through a contract.</div> </div> </div> </div>True Fae are not ephemeral. They are as flesh and blood as manifest stories can be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T11:37:06-08:00","id":420504,"title":"","content":"Also, Mage will obviously lay the whole thing out slightly more clearly than, say, Werewolf (where the focus is appropriately on spirits to the point that Forsaken 2E's version of the GMC ephemeral entity rules has had ghosts and angels cut out of it). When different Arcana let you see different forms of Twilight using your Mage Sight, and ephemera-affecting magic acts differently depending on whether you're using Death or Spirit to do it, we have to.<br /> <br /> The reasons for <i>that</i> go back to game balance issues in Awakening 1e's early design - the reason Moros have Spirit has their inferior Arcanum is based entirely on putting a hard wedge between ghosts and spirits and not letting one Path dominate Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T11:48:57-08:00","id":420514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=420488#post420488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I'm talking about the second edition Numen; I can't even remember if it was called that in first edition, or if there was a specific &quot;ghost-eater&quot; Numen. Either way, we put it in GMC for things like Death spirits, psychopomp-angels, or the rarer and stranger things like astral ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You were right. There's a Numina in Book of Spirits and Book of the Dead, called Ghost Eater.<br /> <br /> Also, for clarification, Numina and Numen are always capitalized?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T14:04:58-08:00","id":420626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/405786-can-werewolves-see?p=420429#post420429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was unfortunately lost in editing for space, but the Essence Thief Numen is supposed to give the entity the ability to percieve the type of essence it gains the ability to eat - a Spirit that can eat ghosts thanks to the Numen is able to see things in ghost-Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Huh, interesting. essence thief seemed like a generic numen- if its ephemeral its lunch, that's an important difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}